  agent-tools refresh           refresh this project's graph, in the right order
  agent-tools status            is a refresh running here? how far along?
  agent-tools stop              stop a run in THIS repo (other projects untouched)
  agent-tools memory status     which backend, what is installed
  agent-tools memory export     memories -> portable Markdown (Obsidian-ready)
  agent-tools memory switch X   change backend machine-wide (claude-mem|agentmemory)
  agent-tools obsidian DIR      export graph + memories into an Obsidian vault
  agent-tools caveman [CMD]     output-token compression: status|install|update|uninstall
  agent-tools update [WHAT]     update all|graphify|memory|caveman|self
  agent-tools help              the reasoning behind every default

Flags (refresh):
  --code-only     AST only, zero LLM, ~1 min
  (default)       code + docs/images semantic pass + community naming
  --deep          as default, but aggressive inferred-edge extraction.
                  Separate cache namespace: the first deep run re-reads
                  every doc. Hours on a large corpus.
  --detach        run in the background, surviving the terminal. Combines
                  with the others: `refresh --deep --detach`.

Memory backend (install-machine):
  --memory=claude-mem   default. light worker on :37701, context injection
  --memory=agentmemory  supervised server, has a bulk transcript importer
  --memory=none         graphify only
  Your choice is remembered in ~/.config/agent-tools/config.

Flags (install-machine):
  --no-caveman          skip the caveman output-compression skill
  -y, --yes       install everything missing without asking (CI / unattended)
      --no-install  never install; just report what is missing
  default         ask before each install; skips (never hangs) when
                  non-interactive

